data carrier_support_split_note: String = "Two decisions, never fused (supersedes the retired MountingRealization enum): what directly carries the board (AssemblyCarrierRealization) and what carries that carrier in the room (CarrierSupportRealization). The same carrier moves lab bench -> freestanding frame -> leased storefront -> purchased building wall without redesigning the compute assembly; support swap never changes assembly or logical-host identity (witness obligation 5). PRIMARY support for the first prototype: FreestandingServiceFrame - floor base/leveling feet, vertical metal uprights, standard horizontal carrier rails, at most a light anti-tip restraint; the building wall carries ZERO normal equipment load. BuildingAttachedRail remains a peer candidate selected only where a site requirement derives it (witness obligation 6: a leased-site policy refusing structural wall alteration removes it). COMMON CARRIER INTERFACE, rev 0, deliberately boring: board-specific hole pattern -> board-family metal adapter plate -> common carrier edge; two upper hooks/captured tabs + one captive lower latch/thumbscrew + handle + manually accessible power/network/BMC connectors; operator sequence drain -> power off -> unplug -> release latch -> lift. REFUSED in rev 0 as convenience dependencies: blind-mate power/network, automatic fluid connectors, custom backplanes, motorized latches, complex sliding rails, a unique frame per board, a board-sized printed structural tray. Bespoke beauty lives in fascia, labels, status lighting, printed airflow pieces, guides, handles, finishes."

