data upstream_decomposition_note: String = "GENERALIZED PRINCIPLE (contamination-access-storage directive section 8): UPSTREAM THE AUTHORITY; DISTRIBUTE THE REALIZATIONS THAT LATENCY, SAFETY, FAULT ISOLATION, OR DISCONNECTION REQUIRE. The test every upstream move must pass: moving something upstream should REMOVE REPEATED AUTHORITY AND MAINTENANCE - not merely move every physical operation farther away. Dust passes (one maintained filtration boundary replaces N server-cleaning obligations). Durable storage passes (one authority survives disposable nodes). Compile scratch FAILS (its authority can disappear, but its locality may still be the cheapest way to satisfy the selected workload) - that asymmetry is why storage was never offloadable as one thing. Standing candidate lanes, each owed its own demand rows: dust (room filtration+envelope upstream / component airflow path + inspection local); physical access (identity, grants, revocation, audit upstream / lock actuation + safe egress local); storage (durable data identity upstream / hot disposable replica or scratch local); power (AC/DC conversion + monitoring upstream / branch protection, connector, board conversion local); cooling (bulk transport + rejection upstream / silicon heat pickup + residual board airflow local); network identity (gateway/address authority upstream / physical last-mile local); boot+firmware (versioned image authority upstream / local bootable recovery copy); monitoring (central event history upstream / local sensors + bounded buffering); time (site/fleet time authority upstream / local oscillator during disconnection); secrets (central semantic authority upstream / short-lived local realization); spares (shared inventory authority upstream / minimal site recovery kit); fire detection (room/zone alarm authority upstream / local source detection where risk requires it)."

data contamination_dependency_note: String = "Dependencies INTRODUCED by upstreaming contamination control (both sides of the ledger, per the dependency law): filter bank, replacement filter media supply, filter dimensions, filter-access clearance, air-handler capacity compatibility, differential-pressure observation, door and penetration sealing, cleaning protocol, filter replacement labor, sealed-envelope integrity. Upstreaming does NOT delete maintenance - it converts N server-cleaning obligations into one room-filter-and-envelope obligation. Probably an excellent trade; the ledger shows both sides. Each becomes an exact PhysicalDependencyEdge with lifecycle and exit plan when the realization is selected."

data access_dependency_note: String = "Dependencies INTRODUCED by electronic access control: access controller, reader family, credential family, lock hardware, door contact, request-to-exit hardware, power supply/battery, credential administration, event-store integration, installer (LicensedTradeDependency), fire/egress approval (RegulatoryApprovalDependency), mechanical-key policy. Likely still beats ordinary keyed access because revocation and audit are valuable - but it is NOT dependency-free. Selection preferences: commodity replaceable hardware over a proprietary building-wide dependency; locally operable over cloud-dependent. Storage-side dependencies for the upstream path: provider, network path, credential, object namespace, retention policy, request/transfer economics, local replica policy, restore/readback mechanism."

