  id: "real-altrad8ud-frame-air",
  assembly_id: "asm-altrad8ud-reference",
  carrier: FlatMetalCarrier,
  support: FreestandingServiceFrame,
  heat_pickup: ForcedAirHeatsink,
  heat_transport: LocalAir,
  heat_rejection: RoomAir,
  power_conversion: PerAssemblyAtxSupply,
  power_adaptation: AtxMultiRailDelivery,
  supply_multiplicity: OneSelectedSupply,
  note: "PRIMARY MINIMAL DESIGN - one board, one ATX PSU, one supported air cooler (Dynatron W1 catalog row; owned D9 AMP pair if board compatibility verifies), one flat removable carrier on the common edge, ordinary manual plugs, optional printed DIMM/VRM shroud only when measurement derives it. No wall load, no fluid, no PDB assumption, no redundant-supply dependency. Proves the generic architecture is simple when hardware presents normal interfaces.",
  status: HypothesisGrade { note: "candidate architecture - its structural/retention/touch-protection demand rows are not yet instantiated; drawn parts are candidates until they are" },
}

data first_witness_obligations: String = "Ten first witnesses, recorded pending the witness carrier (no row below is discharged): (1) selecting ALTRAD8UD air creates no Jade PDB/CRPS dependency; (2) selecting Jade creates its exact PDB/control dependencies; (3) selecting air creates no fluid, CDU, QD, drain, or coolant dependency; (4) removing the last liquid consumer retires the liquid dependency population; (5) moving a carrier between supports (frame/wall/bench/rack) does not change compute-assembly or logical-host identity; (6) a leased-site policy refusing structural wall alteration removes BuildingAttachedRail from candidates; (7) every custom dependency has an exit path and reproduction receipt; (8) every selected artifact traces to at least one exact demand; (9) every selected demand has an admitted realization or remains explicitly unresolved; (10) a decorative facade can be removed without changing cooling, power, or host identity."

data service_pattern_note: String = "GENERIC SERVICE PATTERN (service-boundary directive section 10) - the unifying shape every service lane takes, the physical mirror of the repo's modeling discipline: SelectedConsumer -> ExactServiceDemand -> ExplicitPolicyAndSafetyCeiling -> CandidateProvider -> ExactBinding -> RuntimeObservation -> RetirementWhenLastConsumerDisappears. Instantiated: power (assembly -> watts/current/input-contract demand -> rectifier/distribution/branch binding), storage (job/host -> scratch/cache/durable/block/object demand -> provider binding), cooling (component/zone -> pickup/transport/rejection demand -> thermal service binding), networking (workload -> bandwidth/reachability/isolation demand -> path binding), mounting (assembly -> support/retention/clearance demand -> carrier/support binding). Ledger corollary: centralization deletes repeated dependencies but introduces shared-provider, network-path, and blast-radius dependencies - both sides go in the ledger. GOVERNING PRINCIPLE: move authority and replaceable service contracts upstream to the broadest justified boundary; keep only latency-critical state, fault isolation, safety mechanisms, and irreducible physical interfaces local. TERMINATION CONDITION (not 'everything is centralized'): every dependency lives at the broadest boundary that reduces total lifecycle burden without violating latency, safety, fault isolation, reversibility, or the selected software plan."

data power_acceptance_controls: String = "Twelve power acceptance controls before promoting shared power (witness obligations, none discharged): (1) selecting one direct-12V ALTRAD8UD emits exactly one protected branch; (2) removing the node removes that branch demand; (3) a branch short/overload isolates the branch without losing healthy branches; (4) bus undervoltage produces a typed drain for exactly the associated power domain; (5) one node's inrush cannot reset its neighbors; (6) connector and conductor temperatures stay within admitted limits at sustained peak; (7) board voltage stays inside the pinned input contract under steady load and transients; (8) shared-rectifier efficiency and acoustic receipts beat or fail to beat the per-node ATX baseline honestly; (9) the 12V design emits no 48->12 converter dependency; (10) the 48V design emits exactly one qualified converter dependency per attached 12V board; (11) no unselected board receives a power tap through a board/domain cross product; (12) loss of the last consumer retires the shared branch or domain per policy."

data storage_acceptance_controls: String = "Eight storage acceptance controls (witness obligations, none discharged): (1) a job with scratch demand receives ephemeral storage but no durable volume; (2) a job with artifact output emits an exact durable-object demand; (3) removing the last durable consumer removes the corresponding grant/binding; (4) node loss destroys no authoritative state; (5) shared-storage loss drains only workloads whose selected plan requires it; (6) cache loss causes recomputation or refetch, never data loss; (7) network saturation is a first-class storage-admission failure; (8) local NVMe failure reduces capacity or drains one node, never corrupts a global authority."

data first_frame_architecture_note: String = "FIRST-FRAME TARGET (service-boundary directive section 11): upstream durable object/log authority; site cache/image authority; freestanding compute-service frame containing shared rectifier shelf -> covered branch distribution -> protected manual 12V branches to ALTRAD8UD carriers, plus network switch; each carrier: board + memory + CPU + BMC, local disposable NVMe scratch/cache, no authoritative customer data, ordinary manual power/network disconnects. One mains conversion service, one network fabric, upstream durable storage, local disposable scratch, removable carriers, independently modeled cooling; no wall load, no liquid, no blind-mate, no custom backplane. Meaningfully more decomposed than a conventional server, and still buildable."

data target_architecture_note: String = "TARGET (carrier+dependency directive, verbatim intent): one common service frame; one common removable-carrier interface; one thin board-family adapter per physical board family; optional board-specific airflow geometry only when measurements derive it; zero liquid dependencies until heat routing earns them. The concept is a physical dependency-injection system: board-specific adapter -> common removable carrier -> selectable room support -> selectable service realizations. Acceptance: ALTRAD8UD installs/removes through the simple common interface; Jade uses the same outer interface with its quirks isolated in one vintage adapter; the frame leaves a leased site with minimal restoration; every custom relationship is countable and has an exit; the air realization contains no dormant liquid or redundant-power dependency; support swap preserves logical-host and assembly identity."

data mt_jade_fixture_protocol: String = "Decomposition fixture protocol (extends the compute-infrastructure section 5 arrival checklist - its rows become Stage 0). Stage 0 stock baseline under identical workloads: wall power, throughput, CPU temps, memory/VRM temps where observable, fan RPM, sound level AND spectrum per source, inlet/exhaust temps, throttling, airflow/pressure where practical. Stage 1 externalized acoustic source (remote blower, chassis retained). Stage 2 open carrier with native electrical preserved (plenum variant; owned-D9 variant). Stage 3 direct-liquid feasibility characterization only as study input. Print-first queue: (1) hole/drilling jigs, (2) transition ducts, (3) air-wash shrouds, (4) sensor/cable fixtures, (5) carrier-interface mock-up on a metal primary plane, (6) visual/status components. REFERENCE-FIRST AMENDMENT (carrier+dependency directive): the ALTRAD8UD reference build proves the common frame + carrier interface with normal hardware; the Jade then stress-tests the same interface with proprietary hardware. No vintage selection before receipts; nothing here authorizes purchases, leases, or buildout - section 6 gates unchanged."
